rt to help  people fleeing desperate circumstances  on safe and legal routes and not punish  those who get here because they're  desperate very often her current  proposals are not fit for purpose we  would do things differently my viewers  would say some of them in response would  say yeah but some of these people coming  are terrorists and they are blowing up  people in the united states and that's  why we should have a proper system and  you know i don't disagree we need a  robust system of course we do and there  are good assessment processes in place  unfortunately what i've seen my my  experience with the home office is that  unfortunately it's woefully inadequate  it's been hollowed out in terms of  staffing i think if pretty patel wants  to make the system work better she  should make sure that there is adequate  staffing that processes are adhered to  that the assessments are done in a  timely manner that's not what's  happening at the moment and i think she  needs to look to her own department  rather than fling stones at others how  much does it help to conflate the two  issues of um a dysfunctional asylum  system and what happened in liverpool we  heard from the mayor of liverpool  yesterday and he says there is online  hate and he is doing everything he can  to try to unite the people of liverpool  it's a very difficult time  it is a difficult time and i salute the  people of liverpool and the emergency  services and all those who've been  involved in in responding to this awful  awful incident  and and i do think that liverpool the  people of liverpool are very strong and  they will come together and they will  unite and terrorism isn't per se caused  by asylum seeking there are many routes  into terrorism we have to look at what's  causing the hate and division in our  society there are many causes they all  need to be taken on board and i'm glad  that the mayor of liverpool and others  in liverpool have spoken out so strongly  on the need for unity a